{
  "_comment": "Identity validation vectors (service, domain, environment, build version) shared by the Go, Python and TypeScript platform libraries. Rules: domain and service are matched exactly (no trimming or case folding) against the registry domain vocabulary and service pattern; environment is trimmed and lower-cased, then must be in the registry environment vocabulary (no aliases: 'production' is rejected); version is trimmed, an empty or absent version becomes 'unknown', and the result must match the registry version pattern (a non-matching version is an error, never rewritten). Each invalid case has exactly one invalid field, named in `error` (service | domain | environment | version). Go: go-probe identity-check (obsregistry CheckIdentity + CheckVersion). TypeScript: @platform/frontend-sdk/core initializeCore. Uses only domains present in every registry copy.",
